                <Pad Id="1GKkUuGDEChyv1URThJMo0" Bounds="592,243,401,376" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="In this Process two more operations have been created, of which one is called Grow and the other Shrink. They will increase or decrease the value which is stored in the pad called Size. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Note, how in this patch now differently colored links exist. Everything that is gray is executed for every frame of the runtime, when the node is in your patch, everything in white only once, when the Process is initialized. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Two more colors indicate that also two more operations are available for the Process which can be triggered from the outside. It is important, as decribed in the chapter about pads, that the value gets stored back into a pad, when it has been modified.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;All operations are listed in the patch explorer which can be opened on the left side when clicking on the little gray rectangle with a &quot;P&quot; inside. Don't get confused right now with functions in here which you don't know. What is relevant is that in here you see an overview of all properties (aka pads) and operations that you created.">
